+# CinaConnect v1.0.0 Stable Release Plan
+
+> **Target Release Date:** June 2026  
+> **Release Type:** Major (breaking changes from v0.x)  
+> **Status:** 📋 Planning
+
+---
+
+## 1. Release Goals
+
+v1.0.0 marks the first stable, production-ready release of CinaConnect — a fully self-hosted, white-label Web3 SDK providing wallet connections, multi-chain authentication, payments, smart accounts, and developer tools across web, mobile, and game engines.
+
+### Core Objectives
+
+| Goal | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| **API Stability** | Freeze all public APIs; no breaking changes until v2.0.0 |
+| **Multi-Chain Parity** | All 7 chain adapters at 1.0.0 (Bitcoin, Cosmos, Hedera, NEAR, Starknet, Sui, XRPL) |
+| **Cross-Platform Readiness** | Web, mobile (iOS/Android), and game engine (Unity) SDKs production-ready |
+| **Infrastructure Hardening** | Relay server and RPC proxy production-hardened with monitoring |
+| **Migration Path** | Clear upgrade path from v0.x → v1.0.0 for all 72 packages |
+
+---
+
+## 2. Package Version Strategy
+
+All 72 packages will be bumped to **v1.0.0** unless they are already at a higher major version:
+
+| Version | Packages | Rationale |
+|---------|----------|-----------|
+| **1.0.0** | 65 packages (all currently at 0.1.x/0.2.x) | First stable release |
+| **2.0.0** | 1 package (`@cinaconnect/i18n`) | Already at 2.0.0, bump to 3.0.0 for major alignment |
+| **≥1.0.0** | 9 packages (adapters + nuxt) | Already at 1.0.0, no change |
+
+---
+
+## 3. Release Checklist
+
+### 3.1 Critical Bugs & Fixes
+
+- [ ] All open P0/P1 issues resolved or deferred with clear tracking
+- [ ] Cryptographic implementations (X25519, ChaCha20-Poly1305) independently audited
+- [ ] No known regressions from v0.2.0
+- [ ] All test suites passing on CI (unit + integration + E2E)
+- [ ] Zero lint/typecheck errors across all packages
+
+### 3.2 Testing
+
+- [ ] **Unit tests**: ≥ 104 test files passing (current baseline)
+- [ ] **Integration tests**: Relay ↔ SDK full connection cycle
+- [ ] **E2E tests**: All 6 demo app pages automated via Playwright
+- [ ] **Cross-browser**: Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge (latest 2 versions)
+- [ ] **Cross-platform**: iOS Safari, Android Chrome tested
+- [ ] **Mobile SDKs**: Android Kotlin + iOS Swift native tests passing
+- [ ] **Load testing**: Relay server handles 10K concurrent WebSocket connections
+- [ ] **Performance benchmarks**: Core SDK bundle size < 50KB gzipped
+
+### 3.3 Documentation
+
+- [ ] API reference docs generated via TypeDoc for all public packages
+- [ ] Getting started guide for each platform (Web, React, Next.js, Vue, Mobile, Unity)
+- [ ] Migration guide from Reown AppKit → CinaConnect
+- [ ] Migration guide from v0.x → v1.0.0
+- [ ] Architecture decision records (ADRs) for key design choices
+- [ ] Deployment guides for Relay Server and Keys Server
+- [ ] Security best practices guide
+- [ ] Example projects for each use case
+
+### 3.4 Performance
+
+- [ ] Core SDK tree-shakeable; unused adapters excluded from bundle
+- [ ] Time-to-interactive for demo app < 2s on 3G
+- [ ] WebSocket relay latency p99 < 50ms
+- [ ] RPC proxy cache hit rate > 80%
+- [ ] No memory leaks in long-running connections (> 24h soak test)
+
+### 3.5 Security
+
+- [ ] Dependency audit: `npm audit` / `pnpm audit` clean
+- [ ] All cryptographic code reviewed by ≥ 2 engineers
+- [ ] Secrets management: no hardcoded keys in any package
+- [ ] Relay server: rate limiting, connection limits, input validation
+- [ ] Keys server: TLS enforced, rotation support
+- [ ] Supply chain: lockfile integrity verified, CI pinned versions
+- [ ] Threat model documented for Relay Server and Keys Server
+
+### 3.6 Infrastructure
+
+- [ ] Relay Server deployed on Cloudflare Workers (production config)
+- [ ] RPC Proxy deployed on Cloudflare Workers (production config)
+- [ ] Keys Server health checks configured
+- [ ] Monitoring/alerting for all infrastructure services
+- [ ] Runbook for incident response
+
+### 3.7 Package Publishing
+
+- [ ] All 72 packages have correct `package.json` metadata (description, license, repository, keywords)
+- [ ] npm provenance enabled for all published packages
+- [ ] Changesets applied and version bumps confirmed
+- [ ] Publish dry-run successful
+- [ ] Post-publish smoke tests: install + import each package from npm
+
+---
+
+## 4. Timeline
+
+| Phase | Duration | Start | End | Deliverables |
+|-------|----------|-------|-----|--------------|
+| **Code Freeze** | 1 week | Week 1 | Week 1 | No new features; bug fixes only |
+| **Testing & Audit** | 2 weeks | Week 2 | Week 3 | All checklists green |
+| **RC1 Release** | 1 week | Week 4 | Week 4 | v1.0.0-rc.1 to npm for community testing |
+| **RC Feedback** | 1 week | Week 5 | Week 5 | Address critical RC feedback |
+| **RC2 Release** | 1 week | Week 6 | Week 6 | v1.0.0-rc.2 final candidate |
+| **Stable Release** | 3 days | Week 7 | Week 7 | v1.0.0 published to npm |
+| **Post-Release** | 1 week | Week 7 | Week 8 | Monitor, patch if needed |
+
+**Total estimated timeline: 7-8 weeks**
+
+---
+
+## 5. Risk Assessment
+
+| Risk | Probability | Impact | Mitigation |
+|------|-------------|--------|------------|
+| Critical crypto bug discovered | Low | Critical | Independent audit before RC1; hotfix process ready |
+| Breaking API change required late | Medium | High | Code freeze enforcement; defer to v1.1.0 |
+| npm publish failure for some packages | Low | Medium | Pre-publish validation; batch publish with rollback |
+| Cloudflare Worker limits exceeded | Low | Medium | Pre-scale monitoring; fallback to self-hosted |
+| Community adoption slow | Medium | Low | Marketing push; migration incentives; examples |
+| Dependency security vulnerability | Medium | High | Renovate bot configured; rapid patch process |
+| Mobile SDK compatibility issues | Medium | Medium | Device matrix testing; known-issues documented |
+| Bundle size budget exceeded | Low | Low | Tree-shaking verification; code splitting |
+
+### Risk Matrix
+
+```
+Impact
+  High  │  ● Crypto Bug          │
+        │                        │  ● Late API Change
+  Medium│  ● Deploy Limits       │  ● Mobile Compat
+        │                        │  ● Dependency Vuln
+  Low   │  ● Publish Fail        │  ● Slow Adoption
+        │                        │  ● Bundle Size
+        └────────────────────────┴────────────────
+           Low                High
+                    Probability
+```
+
+---
+
+## 6. Rollout Plan
+
+### Phase 1: RC Release (Week 4-6)
+- Publish `v1.0.0-rc.1` and `v1.0.0-rc.2` to npm under `@next` dist-tag
+- Internal QA testing on all platforms
+- Open beta for trusted partners
+- Collect feedback via GitHub issues
+
+### Phase 2: Stable Release (Week 7)
+- Publish `v1.0.0` to npm under `@latest` dist-tag
+- Tag release on GitHub with comprehensive notes
+- Publish blog post announcing v1.0.0
+- Update all documentation sites
+
+### Phase 3: Post-Release (Week 7-8)
+- Monitor npm downloads, GitHub issues, Discord/community feedback
+- Prepare v1.0.1 patch for any critical issues found
+- Begin v1.1.0 feature planning
+
+### Rollback Plan
+If critical issues are discovered in stable:
+1. Immediately publish `v1.0.1` patch fix
+2. If unfixable quickly, unpublish `v1.0.0`, republish `v0.2.0` as latest temporarily
+3. Communicate status via GitHub, npm, and community channels
+
+---
+
+## 7. Release Team
+
